{"school":{"dbn":"21K239","name":"Mark Twain I.S. 239 for the Gifted & Talented","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"21","district_label":"District 21","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":1290,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"2401 NEPTUNE AVENUE, BROOKLYN, NY 11224","phone":"718-996-6706","website":"www.twain239.com","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/62418","accessibility":"Not Accessible","overview":"Mark Twain Intermediate School for the Gifted and Talented sets itself apart from others because of its dual mission. Students are immersed in an environment of academic rigor blended with a full visual art and performing arts experience, all in an extremely supportive environment. Twain is organized into clusters, or mini-schools, student are grouped with a team of teachers assigned to each. Clusters are scheduled for conference periods to facilitate interdisciplinary planning, data analysis and communication with parents to discuss student progress. This helps teachers and families strategize and focus their instruction to suit individual student needs. Every child is involved in the in-depth study of a Talent area helping students to hone their skills. Mark Twain has invested in innovative teaching strategies that incorporate technology across all classrooms, promoting the development of 21st century skills.  In addition, Mark Twain has embedded the components of Mastery Learning throughout the school community. This approach to learning promotes student progress by through a feedback cycle that focuses on crucial next steps to achieve and deepen mastery of critical skills.","start_time":"08:00am","end_time":"02:19pm","languages":null,"subway":null,"bus":"B36, B74, B82, X28, X38","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":"Coney Island","latitude":40.578666,"longitude":-73.992657,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":